[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186231453 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a02f9513-4eff-5fed-8b27-1eb073c1f7dc" "question-8d772d0d-c3c0-582b-9807-e2b516a97226" "question-3ad87e41-53b3-5b37-8281-b66e69b1893c" "question-5ce73dda-6fa0-5e6a-8244-c7f7fa67bacd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231379 :question/problem "| $x$ | $f(x)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $3$ |\n| $-1$ | $0$ |\n| $0$ | $5$ |\n| $1$ | $-1$ |\n| $2$ | $2$ |\n\nThe table above gives values of $f$ on the set $S=\\{-2,-1,0,1,2\\}.$ Use the table to compute\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\min_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- $\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- $\\min\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\min\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nThe output values in the table are $3,0,5,-1,$ and $2.$\n\nThe largest output is $5,$ and it occurs at $x=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=5\n\\qquad \\textrm{and} \\qquad\n\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=0.\n$$\n\nThe smallest output is $-1,$ and it occurs at $x=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)=-1\n\\qquad \\textrm{and} \\qquad\n\\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)=1.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231454 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d22a2e95-90f5-5fc1-a867-e61a97b4c38b" "question-79c3ad8c-6f33-5a09-8a92-570cf7bc908c" "question-dc43d95b-1383-587c-8ba1-6694a0612d5c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231380 :question/problem "![](images/eb/eb6079ac70816cd56061b8b353cc734176eed1698c50376a2e7a34c40f582a89.png)\n\nLet $S=\\{0,1,2,3,4\\}.$ The graph above shows the value of $f(x)$ for each $x \\in S.$ Use the graph to compute\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\min_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- $\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- $\\min\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\min\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nFrom the graph, the highest point has $y$-coordinate $5,$ and it occurs at $x=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{5}\n\\qquad \\textrm{and} \\qquad\n\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{1}.\n$$\n\nThe lowest point has $y$-coordinate $0,$ and it occurs at $x=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{0}\n\\qquad \\textrm{and} \\qquad\n\\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{4}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-a02f9513-4eff-5fed-8b27-1eb073c1f7dc" :question/id #uuid "a02f9513-4eff-5fed-8b27-1eb073c1f7dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-355248" :question/problem "| $t$ | $h(t)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $-5$ |\n| $0$ | $8$ |\n| $1$ | $2$ |\n| $4$ | $5$ |\n| $7$ | $-3$ |\n\nThe table above gives values of a function $h$ on the set $T=\\{-4,0,1,4,7\\}.$ Compute the following:\n\n${max}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nThe output values are $-5,8,2,5,$ and $-3.$ The maximum output is $8$ (at $t=0$), and the minimum output is $-5$ (at $t=-4$). \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =8 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =0 \\\\ {min}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =-5 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1fdf6472-8e95-570d-bfbc-b65754f7fca4" "answer-field-de64455c-2dd7-5b45-8698-b87b3d241776" "answer-field-6771a7a7-a348-5d16-8f1e-5770d554ff43" "answer-field-a9d8067c-0c37-548f-94b0-8c25c2bb60a6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1fdf6472-8e95-570d-bfbc-b65754f7fca4" :answer-field/id #uuid "1fdf6472-8e95-570d-bfbc-b65754f7fca4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7bb778f6-c4fa-5137-abdb-0ad5c14dacbc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7bb778f6-c4fa-5137-abdb-0ad5c14dacbc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7bb778f6-c4fa-5137-abdb-0ad5c14dacbc" :answer/id #uuid "7bb778f6-c4fa-5137-abdb-0ad5c14dacbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-de64455c-2dd7-5b45-8698-b87b3d241776" :answer-field/id #uuid "de64455c-2dd7-5b45-8698-b87b3d241776" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9182c1d3-01cb-5453-bb22-2f6444b1422e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9182c1d3-01cb-5453-bb22-2f6444b1422e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9182c1d3-01cb-5453-bb22-2f6444b1422e" :answer/id #uuid "9182c1d3-01cb-5453-bb22-2f6444b1422e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6771a7a7-a348-5d16-8f1e-5770d554ff43" :answer-field/id #uuid "6771a7a7-a348-5d16-8f1e-5770d554ff43" :answer-fi