answer-field-3790112f-9ad3-5b4b-ac19-1ba1cf54ede5" "answer-field-e98936a7-13b6-520c-9990-bd1d84f1027a" "answer-field-12e641cb-0fea-53a9-90a9-7fc032f2bb18"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-39c90585-147b-5591-bf04-75354a334afb" :answer-field/id #uuid "39c90585-147b-5591-bf04-75354a334afb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-60eecf3d-93cd-5625-9da7-3d5ee2a20543" :answer-field/choices ["answer-60eecf3d-93cd-5625-9da7-3d5ee2a20543"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60eecf3d-93cd-5625-9da7-3d5ee2a20543" :answer/id #uuid "60eecf3d-93cd-5625-9da7-3d5ee2a20543" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3790112f-9ad3-5b4b-ac19-1ba1cf54ede5" :answer-field/id #uuid "3790112f-9ad3-5b4b-ac19-1ba1cf54ede5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-dfa59b1b-8788-5026-b7df-30dea62754a3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dfa59b1b-8788-5026-b7df-30dea62754a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfa59b1b-8788-5026-b7df-30dea62754a3" :answer/id #uuid "dfa59b1b-8788-5026-b7df-30dea62754a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e98936a7-13b6-520c-9990-bd1d84f1027a" :answer-field/id #uuid "e98936a7-13b6-520c-9990-bd1d84f1027a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b804f278-6e33-5485-b418-c209b0be7d73" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b804f278-6e33-5485-b418-c209b0be7d73"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b804f278-6e33-5485-b418-c209b0be7d73" :answer/id #uuid "b804f278-6e33-5485-b418-c209b0be7d73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-12e641cb-0fea-53a9-90a9-7fc032f2bb18" :answer-field/id #uuid "12e641cb-0fea-53a9-90a9-7fc032f2bb18" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a03d0aa3-f95b-5034-8513-7b38e859b4af" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a03d0aa3-f95b-5034-8513-7b38e859b4af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a03d0aa3-f95b-5034-8513-7b38e859b4af" :answer/id #uuid "a03d0aa3-f95b-5034-8513-7b38e859b4af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186232043 :tutorial/content "In a previous lesson, we learned that $\\max$ and $\\min$ return the largest and smallest *function values,* while $\\arg\\max$ and $\\arg\\min$ return the corresponding *input values.*\n\nIn this lesson, we practice finding $\\max,$ $\\arg\\max,$ $\\min,$ and $\\arg\\min$ from common representations of a function:\n\n- Tables of values\n\n- Graphs" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186232044 :tutorial/content "When a table lists input-output pairs $(x,f(x))$ for $x$ in some set $S,$ we can read:\n\n- $\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ by finding the largest output value in the table.\n\n- $\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ by taking the input value where that largest output occurs.\n\nThe same idea applies to $\\min$ and $\\arg\\min,$ except we look for the smallest output value." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186232045 :tutorial/content "When a graph shows the points $(x,f(x))$ for $x$ in a set $S,$ we can find:\n\n- $\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ by locating the highest point on the graph and reading its $y$-coordinate.\n\n- $\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ by taking the corresponding $x$-coordinate.\n\nThe same idea applies to $\\min$ and $\\arg\\min,$ except we look for the lowest point." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231552 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186231379 :question/problem "| $x$ | $f(x)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $3$ |\n| $-1$ | $0$ |\n| $0$ | $5$ |\n| $1$ | $-1$ |\n| $2$ | $2$ |\n\nThe table above gives values of $f$ on the set $S=\\{-2,-1,0,1,2\\}.$ Use the table to compute\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\min_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x).\n$$"] [17592186231379 :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- $\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- $\\min\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\min\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nThe output values in the table are $3,0,5,-1,$ and $2.$\n\nThe largest output is $5,$ and it occurs at $x=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=5\n\\qquad \\textrm{and} \\qquad\n\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=0.\n$$\n\nThe smallest output is $-1,$ and it occurs at $x=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)=-1\n\\qquad \\textrm{and} \\qquad\n\\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)=1.\n$$"] [17592186231380 :question/problem "![](images/eb/eb6079ac70816cd56061b8b353cc734176eed1698c50376a2e7a34c40f582a89.png)\n\nLet $S=\\{0,1,2,3,4\\}.$ The graph above shows the value of $f(x)$ for each $x \\in S.$ Use the graph to compute\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\min_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x).\n$$"] [17592186231380 :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- $\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- $\\min\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\min\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nFrom the graph, the highest point has $y$-coordinate $5,$ and it occurs at $x=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{5}\n\\qquad \\textrm{and} \\qquad\n\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{1}.\n$$\n\nThe lowest point has $y$-coordinate $0,$ and it occurs at $x=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{0}\n\\qquad \\textrm{and} \\qquad\n\\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{4}.\n$$"] ["question-a02f9513-4eff-5fed-8b27-1eb073c1f7dc" :question/id #uuid "a02f9513-4eff-5fed-8b27-1eb073c1f7dc"] ["question-a02f9513-4eff-5fed-8b27-1eb073c1f7dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-355248"] ["question-a02f9513-4eff-5fed-8b27-1eb073c1f7dc" :question/problem "| $t$ | $h(t)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $-5$ |\n| $0$ | $8$ |\n| $1$ | $2$ |\n| $4$ | $5$ |\n| $7$ | $-3$ |\n\nThe table above gives values of a function $h$ on the set $T=\\{-4,0,1,4,7\\}.$ Compute the following:\n\n${max}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-4}}"] ["question-a02f9513-4eff-5fed-8b27-1eb073c1f7dc" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nThe output values are $-5,8,2,5,$ and $-3.$ The maximum output is $8$ (at $t=0$), and the minimum output is $-5$ (at $t=-4$). \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =8 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =0 \\\\ {min}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =-5 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-a02f9513-4eff-5fed-8b27-1eb073c1f7dc" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-1fdf6472-8e95-570d-bfbc-b65754f7fca4" :answer-field/id #uuid "1fdf6472-8e95-570d-bfbc-b65754f7fca4"] ["answer-7bb778f6-c4fa-5137-abdb-0ad5c14dacbc" :answer/id #uuid "7bb778f6-c4fa-5137-abdb-0ad5c14dacbc"] ["answer-7bb778f6-c4fa-5137-abdb-0ad5c14dacbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7bb778f6-c4fa-5137-abdb-0ad5c14dacbc" :answer/value "8"] ["answer-field-1fdf6472-8e95-570d-bfbc-b65754f7fca4" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-1fdf6472-8e95-570d-bfbc-b65754f7fca4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-1fdf6472-8e95-570d-bfbc-b65754f7fca4" :answer-field/correct "answer-7bb778f6-c4fa-5137-abdb-0ad5c14dacbc"] ["answer-field-1fdf6472-8e95-570d-bfbc-b65754f7fca4" :answer-field/choices "answer-7bb778f6-c4fa-5137-abdb-0ad5c14dacbc"] ["answer-field-de64455c-2dd7-5b45-8698-b87b3d241776" :answer-field/id #uuid "de64455c-2dd7-5b45-8698-b87b3d241776"] ["answer-9182c1d3-01cb-5453-bb22-2f6444b1422e" :answer/id #uuid "9182c1d3-01cb-5453-bb22-2f6444b1422e"] ["answer-9182c1d3-01cb-5453-bb22-2f6444b1422e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9182c1d3-01cb-5453-bb22-2f6444b1422e" :answer/value "0"] ["answer-field-de64455c-2dd7-5b45-8698-b87b3d241776" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-de64455c-2dd7-5b45-8698-b87b3d241776" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-de64455c-2dd7-5b45-8698-b87b3d241776" :answer-field/correct "answer-9182c1d3-01cb-5453-bb22-2f6444b1422e"] ["answer-field-de64455c-2dd7-5b45-8698-b87b3d241776" :answer-field/choices "answer-9182c1d3-01cb-5453-bb22-2f6444b1422e"] ["answer-field-6771a7a7-a348-5d16-8f1e-5770d554ff43" :answer-field/id #uuid "6771a7a7-a348-5d16-8f1e-5770d554ff43"] ["answer-e26bb02d-f4f2-50ea-92ff-5ac151238e8e" :answer/id #uuid "e26bb02d-f4f2-50ea-92ff-5ac151238e8e"] ["answer-e26bb02d-f4f2-50ea-92ff-5ac151238e8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e26bb02d-f4f2-50ea-92ff-5ac151238e8e" :answer/value "-5"] ["answer-field-6771a7a7-a348-5d16-8f1e-5770d554ff43" :answer-field/key "field-3"] ["answer-field-6771a7a7-a348-5d16-8f1e-5770d554ff43" :answer-field/type :answer-fie